course: dictionary
lesson: 11243
title: Worldwide: all over the world
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Worldwide is made of two words, world and wide. The world is the whole planet, and wide means spread far, so worldwide means spread across the whole planet. «The internet began in 1969 by linking a few computers in American universities and grew into a worldwide network.» The clues are linking, grew and network: a network that spreads to every part of the world.
explain: Worldwide can be an adjective or an adverb. As an adjective it describes a noun, as in «a worldwide problem». As an adverb it tells you where something happens: «its films, music and technology spread worldwide». Test it by swapping in all over the world. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: You will often see worldwide with another word: «worldwide famous» means famous in many countries, and «known worldwide» means known in many countries. Be careful with capital letters: «the World Wide Web» is written as three words.
fact: Worldwide means happening or found in all parts of the world.
fact: As an adverb, worldwide means all over the world: «sold worldwide».
fact: «Worldwide famous» means famous in many countries.
fact: Climate change and pandemics are worldwide problems because they affect countries everywhere.
fact: The World Wide Web is written as three words, with capital letters.
exercise: «The internet grew into a worldwide network.» What does worldwide mean here? | Found in only one town | Very old | *Found in all parts of the world | Quiet and slow
exercise: «Its films, music and technology spread worldwide.» Where did they spread? | Only to the next village | Into the sea only | Underground | *All over the world
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to worldwide? | Tiny | *Global | Local | Hidden
test: Which phrase means known in many countries? | Known by nobody | Known locally | Known only at night | *Known worldwide
test: «London Zoo still does research and conservation worldwide.» Where does the zoo do this work? | Under the ground | Only in London | *In many places all over the world | In one room only
exam: Which is the correct way to write the name of the internet's network? | *The World Wide Web | The Worldwide Web | The World-Wide-Web | The Worldwideweb
